{"name":"Seven Veils","hex":"#e3b8bd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 7."]},{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["A numerical value equal to 7; the number following six and preceding eight.","Describing a group or set with seven elements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seven"},{"term":"veils","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of veil"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veils"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance of the Seven Veils","blocks":[{"text":"The Dance of the Seven Veils is the dance performed by Salome before King Herod Antipas in modern stage, literature, and visual arts. It is an elaboration on the New Testament story of the Feast of Herod and the execution of John the Baptist, which refers to Salome dancing before the king, but does not give the dance a name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/PointArmandDanceOftheSevenVeils.jpg/330px-PointArmandDanceOftheSevenVeils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_of_the_Seven_Veils"},{"title":"Salome (opera)","blocks":[{"text":"Salome, Op. 54, is an opera in one act by Richard Strauss. The libretto is Hedwig Lachmann's German translation of the 1891 French play Salomé by Oscar Wilde, edited by the composer. Strauss dedicated the opera to his friend Sir Edgar Speyer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Flickr_-_%E2%80%A6trialsanderrors_-_Richard_Strauss-Woche%2C_festival_poster%2C_1910.jpg/330px-Flickr_-_%E2%80%A6trialsanderrors_-_Richard_Strauss-Woche%2C_festival_poster%2C_1910.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salome_(opera)"},{"title":"Seven Veils (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Seven Veils is a 2023 Canadian drama film written and directed by Atom Egoyan. The film stars Amanda Seyfried as Jeanine, a theatre director who is dealing with repressed trauma as she prepares to mount a production of the opera Salome. Rebecca Liddiard, Douglas Smith, Mark O'Brien, and Vinessa Antoine also star."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/60/Seven_Veils_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Veils_(film)"},{"title":"7","blocks":[{"text":"7 (seven) is the natural number following 6 and preceding 8. It is the only prime number preceding a cube."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg/500px-The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg/1280px-The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg/500px-The_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_%28137274546%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Stomach Dance by Aubrey Beardsley, an interpretation of the Dance of the Seven Veils","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Stomach_Dance_by_Aubrey_Beardsley_(137274546).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Loie_Fuller_Folies_Bergere_02.jpg/500px-Loie_Fuller_Folies_Bergere_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Loie_Fuller_Folies_Bergere_02.jpg/1280px-Loie_Ful